# Copy to benchmarks/.env and fill in the keys under REQUIRED; everything else here
# works as shipped. run.py checks them before it starts anything and lists what is
# missing.
#
# What a run needs follows from its retrieval method (`methods` in
# configs/<benchmark>.toml, or --methods): LoCoMo's `agentic` needs an OpenRouter key
# and a DeepInfra key (embedding and rerank); the other three benchmarks'
# `llm_multiround` needs the same two keys but no rerank; `--methods keyword` runs on
# the OpenRouter key alone. See benchmarks/README.md, "Which keys you need".

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The EverOS servers this harness starts: extraction (ADD) and the retrieval decider.
# A server whose LLM is unconfigured aborts at startup, and `everos init` only writes a
# blank template, so the key belongs here rather than in each generated everos.toml.
EVEROS_LLM__API_KEY=
# Embedding and rerank use EverOS's defaults: Qwen3-Embedding-4B and Qwen3-Reranker-4B
# on DeepInfra, so only their keys go here (one DeepInfra key works for both).
# Embedding serves every method except keyword; rerank serves agentic, LoCoMo's method:
# without it every agentic search fails. Leave one empty only when no method you run
# needs it; run.py refuses to start rather than let ADD spend on a store the chosen
# method cannot search. Set EVEROS_EMBEDDING__BASE_URL / __MODEL (or EVEROS_RERANK__*)
# only to serve them somewhere else.
EVEROS_EMBEDDING__API_KEY=
EVEROS_RERANK__API_KEY=
# Answer and judge stages. The same OpenRouter key works for both; several keys,
# comma-separated, are rotated round-robin.
ANSWER_API_KEY=
JUDGE_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Endpoints -- the shipped values match the keys above
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model choice does NOT belong here (the optional decider override at the end is the
# one exception): it lives in configs/<benchmark>.toml, which is the single source of
# the experiment's identity. A model name in this file was silently overridden by the
# config at launch while still being what the run record reported.
EVEROS_LLM__BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
EVEROS_LLM__TIMEOUT_SECONDS=300
ANSWER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
JUDGE_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# Engine-wide cap on concurrent extractions. The default of 20 throttles a bulk ingest
# long before the machine does -- each slot spends its time waiting on a remote call.
EVEROS_OME__MAX_CONCURRENT_RUNS=64

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Paths (all optional -- every one has a working default)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LEFT EMPTY ON PURPOSE. Each of these has a default that works out of the box, and
# an empty value falls through to it. A placeholder like `/path/to/Evaluation` would
# NOT: it is a set variable, so it wins over the default, and the run then writes to
# a directory literally called `/path/to/...`. A value that looks configured but is
# not is worse than no value at all.
#
# `bash benchmarks/download_data.sh <benchmark>` writes to the defaults below. Fill one
# in only when your copy of the data lives somewhere else.

# Datasets. Default: benchmarks/data/<the file named below>.
#   locomo        -> benchmarks/data/locomo10.json
#   longmemeval   -> benchmarks/data/longmemeval_s.json
#   subtlememory  -> benchmarks/data/subtlememory/      (a directory)
#   evermembench  -> benchmarks/data/evermembench.json
BENCH_DATA_LOCOMO=
BENCH_DATA_LONGMEMEVAL=
BENCH_DATA_SUBTLEMEMORY=
BENCH_DATA_EVERMEMBENCH=

# LoCoMo's gold audit, which the judge stage re-judges the disputed questions against.
# Default: benchmarks/data/locomo-audit-errors.json.
BENCH_DATA_LOCOMO_AUDIT=

# EverMemBench only: its raw release, read to recover session names the converted
# file does not carry. Default: benchmarks/data/raw/EverMemBench-Dynamic.
EVERMEMBENCH_RAW_ROOT=

# Where runs are written. Default: benchmarks/results/<Dataset>/. Point this at a
# directory outside the repository when the filesystem holding it is near capacity --
# a full disk surfaces as [Errno 28] on every answer write, which is retried and then
# recorded as a failed question rather than as an outage.
BENCH_EVAL_ROOT=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The multi-round retrieval decider (optional; llm_multiround only)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave BOTH empty and the decider runs the model from [llm] -- the single-model
# setup, which needs no extra configuration and is what a first run should use.
#
# Each configs/<benchmark>.toml comes pre-filled with its recommended decider (the one
# behind the published number). To use it, set BENCH_DECIDER_BASE_URL to an
# OpenAI-compatible endpoint that serves that model; set BENCH_DECIDER_MODEL as well
# only to run a different one. A name the endpoint does not serve returns 404 on every
# call, and the retrieval loop then falls back to a fixed core and still reports a
# complete result. run.py probes the decider at startup and refuses to run rather than
# let that happen quietly.
#
# LoCoMo's decider (deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731) is served by OpenRouter: set
# BENCH_DECIDER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1 and BENCH_DECIDER_API_KEY to the
# same OpenRouter key as above.
BENCH_DECIDER_MODEL=
BENCH_DECIDER_BASE_URL=
# Any non-empty value for a self-hosted server; a hosted API needs its real key.
BENCH_DECIDER_API_KEY=EMPTY
